<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niger bend</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> bend is the great northward curve of the Niger River in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, where the river reaches the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timbuktu">Timbuktu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao">Gao</a>. Its waterways and trading cities were key strategic assets. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> extended its control there in the late thirteenth century, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a>'s river fleet later gave it dominance over the region.</p></div>
